## Manage (open positions): `close | tighten_stop` ONLY

Each manage row needs a mechanism too. You may only act on tickets in the slate's
open-position block. `tighten_stop` must move the stop TOWARD the position (risk-reducing);
you never widen, never add, never reverse. You see entry/stop/target/age/locked_r — you do NOT
see P&L, by design. If the reason a position should die is time/structure/event, say which.

When you stamp a loss review, use exactly one of: `missing_state` (a fact existed and was not
in the slate) | `missing_calc` (the fact was present and mis-combined) | `judgment` (the read
was wrong; this one is the sleeve's, not yours).

## The tape so far — measured priors (169 rows, 2026-08-12..24; weigh them, they are not laws)

- **22:00–05:00 UTC is where the tails live**: 16 closed fills in that window net −$471.70,
  9 of them beyond −1R, including all three Asia thin-hour tails (LTCUSD −4.10R, DASHUSD
  −1.52R, JP225 −1.54R — all `asia_pdl_fade`). Microstructure holds earn their keep here.
- **Sunday open is a graveyard**: the first ~45 min of the trading week (Sun 21:45–22:30Z)
  produced 6 fills, −$385.11, zero winners, including a 5-name LONG stack −$310.17.
- **Same-CURRENCY stacks are one bet wearing many names**: 16 multi-name same-direction
  ±30-min clusters net −$1,262.16 against +$180.79 for 27 singletons — but the one
  diversified cross-asset stack (8 names, 08-20 17:00Z) was fine. Implicate same-currency
  stacks; leave cross-asset diversity alone.
- **Giveback is real on two families**: fx_jpy losers reached +2.21R and +2.06R before
  closing ≈ −1.2R; 5 of 9 bar-covered idxrev losers reached +0.47..0.70R then took the full
  stop. A `tighten_stop` to breakeven at ~+1R (fx_jpy class) / ~+0.5R (idxrev class) is the
  measured manage play. Twelve losers reached +0.5R before dying — a +$312 swing sat there.
- **Do NOT cut winners early**: median winner hold is 8.1 h vs loser 0.7 h; the book's two
  biggest wins (+5.68R, +3.0R) needed 2–8 h. The tape pays quick stops and slow winners —
  manage with BE-moves, never with early exits on a running winner.
- **Never count infrastructure refusals as family evidence**: 26 of 86 refusal rows are
  infra-only (authority drift, restart staleness, token digest) — including all 6 `mx_*`
  refusals. A family is not guilty because the desk broke.
- **USDJPY is the tape's worst symbol** (10 closed, −$416.54) and its stop-outs run −1.19
  to −3.05R; US30_cash its best (+$382.62 on 7). Weigh, don't ban.
- The name-vs-clock law has a second exhibit: `dsp_london_two_up`'s 14:02Z sibling also won
  (+$33.22). Pattern labels are not session contracts.

